data.content:
## Breaking Changes in Microsoft.OpenApi v2 (used by .NET 10)

Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0 upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which targets OpenAPI 3.1 / JSON Schema 2020-12. Here are the key breaks and fixes:

### 1. `OpenApiString` / `IOpenApiAny` removed
The `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` namespace is gone. Primitive values are now `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode`.

```csharp
// Before:
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After:
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `OpenApiReference.Type` changed
`ReferenceType` enum → `OpenApiConstants` string-based type, and the property is now `Type` of type `Uri`.

```csharp
// Before:
Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }

// After:
Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2", "securitySchemes")
```

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` no longer a `Dictionary`
It's now a class with a `Schemes` dictionary.

```csharp
// Before:
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After:
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { Schemes = { [oAuthScheme] = scopes } }
};
```

### 4. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI 3.1 uses JSON Schema's `type` array. Use the `Type` flags enum:

```csharp
// Before:
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (to add nullable):
property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type | JsonSchemaType.Null;

// To remove nullable (your case):
property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
```

(`JsonSchemaType` is in `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models`.)

### Full corrected code:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference("oauth2", "securitySchemes")
    };
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { Schemes = { [oAuthScheme] = scopes } }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type = property.Value.Type & ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

### Summary of namespace changes
| Old | New |
|-----|-----|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` | `System.Text.Json.Nodes` |
| `OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. | `JsonValue.Create(...)` |
| `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` | `new OpenApiReference("id", "securitySchemes")` |
| `schema.Nullable` | `schema.Type` with `JsonSchemaType.Null` flag |
